## 5. Autonomy

The A-scale labels were supplied without definitions; I read them as: A0 advises only; A1 executes only under per-action human approval/supervision; A2 executes multi-step work unattended inside pre-authorized bounds; A3 additionally verifies its own results independently before proceeding; A4/A5 delegate authority and set strategy. This reading is mine and is stated so it can be corrected.

| Level | Label | Evidence and reasoning |
|---|---|---|
| A0 Advisory | **OBSERVED** | Chat text generation; `PlannerAnalyst` is advisory/non-executable and hard-blocked in the Router (S2 `planner_analyst_agent.py`, `router.py`). |
| A1 Assisted Execution | **OBSERVED** | Tasks execute real tools through the governed chain; MODERATE+ actions require explicit human approval; approvals persist and resume Tasks (S1/S2). |
| A2 Bounded Autonomy | **PARTIALLY OBSERVED** | SAFE/LOW operations auto-execute within sandbox and gateway bounds; multi-subtask Tasks run unattended in a background thread; timed standing grants allow repeated MODERATE actions without re-approval. *Why only partial:* planning is rule-based over a fixed message→TaskType table; chains are linear; no recovery from interruption; the bounds that exist are coarse (D5 gap) and not independently verified. |
| A3 Verified Autonomy | **ABSENT** as a system property | Verification exists for two tools plus return-code evaluators; INCONCLUSIVE/NOT_ATTEMPTED leave subtasks DONE; no requirement/evidence record; Task `COMPLETED` ignores verification state (D3 keeps it execution-oriented by decision). Nothing verifies *outcomes against goals*. |
| A4 Delegated | **ABSENT** | No authority delegation mechanism (§12). |
| A5 Strategic | **ABSENT** / FUTURE TARGET | No goal-setting or strategic entities (§17). |

**Highest level supported by evidence: A1 firmly, A2 partially. Not A3.**

